implementationPlan.description:
The fix, in scripts/local-runner/guest-session.mjs, inside relay/pump only. Use the existing stop/controller/timer ownership and add no second queue. guest-bridge.mjs, GUARD/pump in guest-supervisor.py and the certify modules stay untouched.
- child 'close': code 0 succeeds when stdout ended cleanly and one observation arrived. Hello is implied: receive() admits an observation only after hello. Drop the `session.pending.length > 0` condition. A request still pending at that point was abandoned by the guest's own terminal observation and EOF.
- pump: `while (session.pending.length > 0 && !session.closing)`, so no queued request is dispatched, and no health probe or forward starts, once teardown began. In its catch, a TIMEOUT or a reply-write error that arrives after session.closing is a teardown artifact: stop dispatching without a code. Before closing, the codes are unchanged (SESSION_TIMEOUT / SESSION_PROVIDER_FAILED).
- Unchanged:
  - the job-frame write's failure handling (fail closed: a guest cannot have started a job whose frame failed);
  - the caller-abort path (SESSION_ABORTED until settle);
  - stop's kill timer (a provider still running timeoutMs after teardown is SESSION_TIMEOUT);
  - every receive() and decoder guard (hello once, observation once, nothing after it, id replay, MAX_PENDING_REQUESTS, trailing bytes at EOF);
  - `failure ??=` first-failure-wins, so cancellation never erases a prior failure.
- Rewrite runGuestSession's JSDoc 'no owed reply' sentence. At a clean finish, in-flight forwards see their signal abort and queued requests are never forwarded. No reply is written after the finish. Nothing reports that an upstream effect was undone: an aborted forward may already have acted.
- The result shape stays {observation, executionReady: false}. agent-lifecycle.mjs (runAgentJob) reads only observation, and AJ5's no-observation row stays a violation.
Then the focused run: `node --test scripts/tests/local-runner-bridge.test.mjs` is green, including H1-H8.
Error handling: only fixed SESSION_* codes, with no guest bytes or upstream text in any error.

implementationPlan.note:
